# Optional. Everything has a safe default; Mock mode needs no tenant and no credentials.
# The shared settings file is ~/Development/.env (mode 600; STANDALONE_ENV overrides the path), read by every standalone app.
# In Mock this lab reads one optional key from it:
# CAL_LAB_MODE=mock               # the mode a new workspace opens in: mock (default) or live (live also needs the opt-in below)
# Per-run settings (shell, not the shared file; the shared file holds no PORT):
# PORT=5600                       # must be in 5600-5699 (Docker publishes 5601 by default)
# CALAB_BIND=127.0.0.1            # loopback only unless you set this on purpose (the container does)
# ALLOW_MOCK_SIGNIN=1             # the owner's opt-in to the mock persona sign-in (scripts/run.sh and Docker set it)
# IDP=mock                        # mock (default). Anything else turns mock sign-in off.
# CAL_ALLOW_LIVE=1                # the owner's opt-in to SELECT live mode (see the live block at the end)
# Live mode (step 3, owner only, identity provider only; UNVERIFIED on a real tenant). All of these, in the shell for the first two:
# CAL_ALLOW_LIVE=1                # and IDP=pingone (mock turns live off; any other value is refused)
# IDP=pingone
# The shared file ~/Development/.env (or STANDALONE_ENV) must also hold PINGONE_ENVIRONMENT_ID, PINGONE_REGION, PINGONE_CLIENT_ID and PINGONE_CLIENT_SECRET.
# The lab reads them with util.parseEnv for live.js only and never copies them into the environment. Docker stays Mock.
# CAL_LIVE_TEST_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/<environment id>   # tests and e2e only: a fake PingOne on loopback
